  {
    "episode_id": 94779,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/4/94779.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 14,
    "turn_text": "Tutor, thank you. And by the way, when I saw you in Grand Rapids and then shortly thereafter, Ruby Garcia was brutally murdered. Boy, that hits close to home for me. I mean, we're parents of four children. Our youngest daughter is about the same age as Ruby. I just can't imagine what that would be like as a parent and families here of Ruby Garcia. But look, The so-called border bill that the Democrats were proposing that I voted against, it didn't solve the problem. This problem is very solved, but you go back to when President Trump was in office, he had policies in place that had secured the border in a way that we hadn't seen in a decade, in terms of the flow of illegal migrants coming across the southern border. And it was on day one of the Biden administration. I mean, I was on The Western steps there of the US Capitol watching Joe Biden get inaugurated in January of 21. And then hours later, he goes down to the Oval Office through executive order. He reversed policies that were working under President Trump. It's as simple as that. It was the remain in Mexico policies. It was the wall. It was policies that truly had secured the southern border. The problem with that bill that I voted against the Democrats are saying would have would have secured this on board. The fact is it did not. And the policies didn't secure the southern border. And furthermore, I don't believe that President Biden would have enforced any of the policies we might even pass right now in Congress because he's lawless. He's violating the law. They don't want to solve the problem. The only reason Joe Biden went down to the border here several weeks ago, if you remember, he finally made a trip down the southern border, it wasn't because he wanted to solve the border crisis. He's got a political crisis. He knows this is the number one issue facing voters across the country, across Michigan, and it's not just Republicans, this is a number one issue now with Republicans, independents, and Democrats as well. He has a political crisis. They don't know what to do, but they want to see open borders. I think that's That's something we forget about this.",
