    "turn_text": "Well, I think Mr. President has a huge problem in Michigan, and you take a look at his numbers in Michigan. Look at his numbers nationally. He's the most unpopular president we've had going back 70 years at the same point in time in presidency. I remember the days of Jimmy Carter, the late 70s. There's a lot of parallels. We had this very weak president in Jimmy Carter, this very weak president in Joe Biden. You look, we had inflation in the late 70s. Now, inflation is now rising, gas prices. We had high mortgage rates. And then we had the geopolitical craziness was back then it was iran again now it's iran attacking israel through through uh through homos and has the law so you see these parallels and i'll tell you what if you look what happened in the the fall of uh of nineteen eighty when one reagan ran against jimmy carter it was a massive landslide and by the way We look back on political history and say, oh, yeah, Reagan won by a landslide against Carter. I will tell you that nobody saw that landslide coming against Jimmy Carter. That was a neck-and-neck race all the way until $48 for election day when then the pollster started to see this massive shift to Reagan. I think we're seeing something underneath right now going off the electorate with Joe Biden and President Trump. I think you're going to see a big shift as this race closes out. where voters are saying, good grief. We cannot stand. This country can't stand anymore. The world can't stand a weak leader like President Biden anymore. I think it's going to be a big night for President Trump.",
