    "turn_text": "You know, I was in a meeting last weekend. Someone said something really interesting that I hadn't really considered because, you know, I was just a baby when Carter was president, but they made a very interesting point. They said, you know, Carter was an unpopular president, but he was in his 50s. He was young. There was still a, a understanding that he was a capable person, that there was a, a mental capacity there of sorts. But Joe Biden is in a worse situation in his, in his 80s. And he is definitely not with it. I mean, if you watch a video of Joe Biden from just a few years ago compared to today, you can see the mental decline. So I think that this is a, a two-fold problem for him. It's not just that he's unpopular, like Jimmy Carter. Jimmy Carter was still young. There's a lot to be said for still being young.",
