    "turn_text": "Well, I think, too, that's a great point. I remember I was sworn in to the United States Senate by then Vice President Joe Biden. You know, the Vice President swears in US senators. I was newly elected in 14. Joe Biden was Barack Obama's Vice President. He swore me in. I mean, I remember that Joe Biden passed when, just in terms of his capacities, age catches us all. Somebody just does. It's just a fact of life as the sands of time go through the hourglass. And the problem that Biden has, the Democrats, is that every day that he goes by is a day that he's getting older. Time is not on his side, it's working against him. And he needs to have the self-awareness to step down. Frankly, everybody needs to cut that point. I mean, why is it that you take a look at executive boards, pilots, there's requirements for age. that says you can't serve past a certain period of time. Now I'm not suggesting we have to put a time limit for President of the United States, but you got to be self-aware saying, I'm past my time. It's time to retire. And that's why I think you're seeing younger voters now who typically are more lean Democrat are fleeing the Democrat Party and are moving towards the Republican side of the ledger here because they can't imagine Joe Biden serving four more years when he's really incapable of doing it now.",
