  {
    "episode_id": 94779,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/4/94779.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 31,
    "turn_text": "I've heard so many people that have said, you know, I'm an independent now. I don't want to identify as either one. And yet I'm voting for Trump. So I find it very interesting to see what is going on. I think people don't like the idea of the party system and being pulled to one side and having to identify as something, you know, this generation is like, I don't want to commit generation. but they are committing. They're just not openly committing. I think that that silent majority that we saw in 2016 is back and it's bigger than it was. But we'll see. I mean, polls are hard to, they're hard to analyze. Let's talk about",
