    "turn_idx": 33,
    "turn_text": "to wait one point on that. He just made a really good point. Is that is if somebody told me once when you look at elections, voters look at their ballot and they've got to make a choice. But I think a really important point here is when you talk about a candidate, don't compare a candidate to the Almighty, compare them to the alternative. It's going to be a binary choice here between Donald Trump and Joe Biden. And yeah, I know there'll be some young people that may have some problems with President Trump. But they've got huge problems with Joe Biden. And this is a binary choice. One of these two men is going to be the next President of the United States for the next four years. We'll have a profound impact on the generations to come. That's why I think you're going to see these younger voters say, well, I cannot vote for Joe Biden. I'm supporting Donald Trump.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_09",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
