    "turn_text": "Well, as you know, Tutor, we're both big fans of President Trump and worked with him in the past. And I think what he came out and said there, you look at what, kind of unpack what he said in that video. He said, first and foremost, we're going to protect families that have in vitro fertilization. That's a pro-family, pro-baby, pro-America kind of stands for families that struggle with infertility. That's a good thing he came out and said, we're going to protect that. Then you said, you know, we're going to have exceptions for rape, incest, and life in the mother. So many voters want to make sure those exceptions are in place in terms of what they see this very tough and contentious issue. We're both pro-life, dude. I know where you're at. I know where I'm at. Here's a father of four and grandparents of six. But I think President Trump really laid out the right position here, and then he talked a lot about the extreme contrast between where Democrats are at on the issue of life. They will put no limits on abortion up until the moment of birth when a baby can feel pain. That's out of step with the vast majority of Americans, even pro-choice Americans, say that's too extreme. So I think the way the president laid that out was right. And I think we needed to look at having reasonable limits on late-term abortions, with exceptions. But I think President Biden set the right tone here. Excuse me, President Trump set the right tone here, but paint in that contrast of the radical position the Democrats take on the issue of abortion. We're at a step with most countries in the world except for countries like North Korea and China as it relates to protections for the unborn.",
