    "turn_text": "Yeah. Well, I mean, you look at Gretchen Whitmer here in the state of Michigan, she can't talk about anything above the waist. She can only talk to you about things that happen in your body below the waist. And that is abortion, abortion, abortion. But look at what she was able to accomplish in the state of Michigan. And I do believe that this is because we were not ready for stops. We were not ready for that discussion. And we had been talking to people on the subject politically and not culturally. And so instead of having Well, she claimed she was going to restore Roe in the state of Michigan. This isn't Roe. We have no limits on abortion in the state of Michigan. We have no parental consent. There are no safeguards for young women in the state of Michigan. And so I think that's where we have to say, OK, we have to be honest about this as Republicans and figure out how to make sure that there aren't we haven't gone beyond what we had for 50 years that we haven't gone to the most extreme North Korean proposals in North Korean stance on abortion but that is what we've done in the state of Michigan and so it to me it's very important that we talk about this issue from the standpoint of how do we reduce that number of by supporting families in different ways. And if you look at since the Dobbs decision, we've had a massive increase in abortions across the country. So let's talk about policies that support families. And that's what Donald Trump has been so good about doing, talking about childcare for federal employees, talking about paternity leave, maternity leave, all of these things that are helping families to get that kickstart once they have that baby come home in that tough situation of having your first kid and then being able to, okay, we're going to come around this baby. We're going to still have the financial means to do that. And we're going to get a good kickstart on this baby's life. I just think there's so many things as Republicans we can focus on. And I love the fact that that's the kind of people who I think will be in office come November, the election in November.",
