    "turn_text": "myths we have to continue to dispel is I think sometimes voters think well the Republicans have all the money the Democrats don't it's absolutely false I mean if you look at every major Senate race right now across the country the Democrats have the money we've got to always work uphill against an avalanche of cash and that the left throws at these candidates. But I'll tell you, I mean, you always hear tutors, every election is the most important election of our generation. This one really is. I would challenge anybody listening, say, find me a more important election looking back in history than this one coming into 24 and the importance of the US Senate. The reason the Senate's so important and the reason Michigan's so important is because if we don't win back control of the US Senate, the Democrats are going to blow up the legislative filibuster. There were two Democrat senators that saved the legislative filibuster in the last Congress. It was Joe Manchin and Kirsten Sinema. Joe, of course, of West Virginia, Sinema of Arizona. They've both announced their retirements. So if the Democrats have control, they will what they call nuke the filibuster. And then it's a simple 51 vote majority to pass any laws that they want. They'll be basically unbridled. And what will they do if they have 51 votes to pass a law? First of all, the Roe v. Wade would be codified if you're a pro-life voter Roe v. Wade is codified. It would usurp any powers of the states and Roe v. Wade would be codified. But chilling, here's what happens, is DC becomes a state That's two Democrat senators forever. They moved the Supreme Court from nine justices to 13 because they don't like the conservative court. And the founding fathers didn't say the Supreme Court's nine. They left at the Congress to define the size of the Supreme Court. So they pack it with 13, turn it, lurch to the left. And then third, they passed Nancy Pelosi and Chuck Schumer's dream bill, which is called HR1. That's a house bill. They would pass, move to the Senate and pass it. And that's a federal takeover of elections. That means if a state wants to put voter ID in place, that's gone because it disenfranchises minorities. They would allow all mail-in ballots everywhere mandating it. It would take away the state's rights for means and methods of administering elections. So this is a massive power grab. And that is teed up. Adam Schiff, who's a Democrat running for the United States Senate in California, actually laid this out in chilling detail in writing. about what they plan to do if they get control. So this is not just about a policy fight. This would be a complete takeover, a power grab by the left, and we have a hard time ever getting back in the majority again for a generation, if not more.",
