    "turn_text": "Right, and put further color around that tutor. That's what they call the legislative filibuster. In other words, it's a 60 vote threshold to get something passed, dropping some of the majority. But in a 50-50 Senate, see, that's where we were after Joe Biden was elected president, we had 50 Republicans and 50 Democrats in the US Senate. So we were literally a coin toss, 50-50. Kamala Harris is the tie-breaking vote. If you go back to your high school government days, they tell you what happens when the Senate is tied, well, the Vice President of the United States breaks the tie. Kamala Harris has now broken more ties than any Vice President in our nation's history. So we've had 47 Vice Presidents since our great nation was founded. She is now number one in tie-breaking votes. She surpassed John Adams and John Calhoun, who both served eight years as vice",
